Atlas overlay patch 0105: ui/default-system-theme
Why: the chrome of Atlas is exact (the WolOS accent on the privacy glyph, the star, the rest mark, the focus ring)
 only in a profile that carries the preference extensions.theme.system_theme=1; WolOS seeds it
 (crates/core theme/helium.rs), but a profile that was made another way (a new profile, a copied one, a web
 app) showed the engine's white neutrals and blue #5578F4 (ATLAS-E2E-09). The default of the preference is
 ui::GetDefaultSystemTheme(); it is now the GTK theme, which is what the seed asks for. Nothing else changes: the
 choice of the Linux UI toolkit already treated the default as GTK.
Files: ui/linux/linux_ui_factory.cc
Test filter: AtlasKitSystemTheme (journey); journey: start with an empty profile, the privacy glyph is #7452F5
Rebase risk: L (one return value in a short function)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied (dev slot 8)

--- a/ui/linux/linux_ui_factory.cc
+++ b/ui/linux/linux_ui_factory.cc
@@ -188,7 +188,10 @@
 
   switch (base::nix::GetDesktopEnvironment(env.get())) {
     default:
-      return SystemTheme::kDefault;
+      // Atlas: the browser follows the system theme (WolOS's GTK theme and its
+      // accent) in every profile, not only in one that was given the
+      // preference when it was made (QA-E2E-09).
+      return SystemTheme::kGtk;
   }
 }
 
